<Project>
  <!-- The doc-comment gate's two suppressions (#430, #490), applied HERE rather than in
       Directory.Build.props so a project can opt out of them.

       Directory.Build.props is imported before the project's own content, so a project
       cannot set a flag that props would see. Directory.Build.targets is imported AFTER
       it, so the condition below reads a property the project set for itself. NoWarn is
       consumed by the compiler well after both, so setting it here is equivalent to
       setting it there for every project that does not opt out.

       See Directory.Build.props for why CS1591 (missing XML comment) and CS1573 (missing
       <param>) are suppressed by default, and for the six projects that opt out because
       they enforced both as build errors before the repo-wide GenerateDocumentationFile
       existed. Those projects set:

           <VouchfxDocumentEveryPublicMember>true</VouchfxDocumentEveryPublicMember>

       Suppression is the quiet default and requiring documentation is the explicit,
       per-project exception: the gate this repository wants is malformed-or-wrong
       documentation, not absent documentation, and only the projects whose public
       surface is a published contract hold the stricter line.

       THIS FILE IS SILENTLY SHADOWABLE, AND NOTHING WOULD REPORT IT. MSBuild imports only the
       NEAREST Directory.Build.targets found walking up from a project, so a new one added under
       tests/, src/ or examples/ would replace this file for every project beneath it rather than
       adding to it — turning CS1591 (missing XML comment) back into a build error across those
       assemblies with no diagnostic naming the cause. The pattern is already live one directory
       down: tests/Directory.Build.props exists and has to re-import the root explicitly via
       GetPathOfFileAbove for exactly this reason. A sibling added here must carry the same
       import. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(VouchfxDocumentEveryPublicMember)' != 'true'">
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CS1573</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
